"""Skip a doomed conservative clearance pass using its exact endpoint tests.

The adaptive allocator first tries a conservative weighted-distance band. A
single incompatible prescribed endpoint rejects that entire band, after which
the directional allocator is used. Check those same endpoints first, against
every original peer sample. A passing precheck accepts nothing: the complete
conservative allocator must still run. A failure only avoids work whose result
is already known to be rejected. Sampling and the directional fallback stay
unchanged. This is an opt-in experiment, not a public asset migration.
"""
